<title>INDIA: Indian gold up on speculative buying, poor supply.</title>
<headline>Indian gold up on speculative buying, poor supply.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian gold prices rose in early trade on Friday on speculative buying and reduced supply, dealers said. Prices of gold biscuits (116.50 gramme) rose by 100 rupees to 59,200 rupees per piece.</p>
<p>They were up by 300 rupees on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Reports that custom officials had seized contraband gold worth 30 million rupees at the border in northern India helped firm up sentiment in early trade,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>&quot;Physical buying however remained low and there may be some profit-taking later in the day,&quot; he said.  </p>
